K550W in a 57.5 mm minimum-diameter airframe gets you to 3,139.4 m, well past your 2,500 m floor, with about 1,250 m of drift in 2 m/s wind.
2.61 kg liftoff, 20.9:1 thrust-to-weight, rail exit 25.9 m/s, landing 4.1 m/s on a 1.6 m chute, margin 1.15 cal.
The 0.30 kg of nose ballast is what makes it stable: the fins alone left it near 0.5 cal, and enlarging them pulled the CG back as fast as the CP went aft.
