{
  "name": "57.5 mm K550W club rocket",
  "stages": [
    {
      "name": "Sustainer",
      "components": [
        {"type": "nosecone", "shape": "ogive", "length_m": 0.22, "diameter_m": 0.0575, "wall_thickness_m": 0.0015, "material": "Fiberglass", "shoulder_length_m": 0.07},
        {"type": "bodytube", "name": "Booster", "length_m": 0.7, "outer_diameter_m": 0.0575, "wall_thickness_m": 0.001, "material": "Fiberglass",
         "contents": [
           {"type": "parachute", "diameter_m": 1.6, "cd": 0.8, "deploy_event": "apogee", "material": "Ripstop nylon", "position_from_top_m": 0.08},
           {"type": "motor_mount", "outer_diameter_m": 0.0555, "length_m": 0.42, "wall_thickness_m": 0.0006, "material": "Fiberglass",
            "motor": {"manufacturer": "AeroTech", "designation": "K550W", "delay_s": null},
            "overhang_m": 0.01, "centering_ring_count": 2, "centering_ring_material": "Plywood (birch)"},
           {"type": "trapezoidal_fins", "count": 4, "root_chord_m": 0.2, "tip_chord_m": 0.08, "span_m": 0.09, "sweep_m": 0.07, "thickness_m": 0.003, "material": "Carbon fiber", "offset_from_aft_m": 0.015},
           {"type": "mass", "name": "nose ballast", "mass_kg": 0.3, "position_from_top_m": 0.12}
         ]}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
</design>

M1378LR in a 57.5 mm minimum-diameter airframe reaches 6,147.2 m, about 20,200 ft, so the 20,000 ft goal is met within a percent.
6.05 kg liftoff, 23.1:1 thrust-to-weight, rail exit 33.9 m/s, landing 3.4 m/s on a 2.8 m chute, margin 4.90 cal.
Note for the team: fin area moved apogee by over a kilometre between my first two drafts, so cut the fins to these dimensions exactly. This is an L2 motor, so it needs a certified flyer supervising.
