AeroTech I200W in a 41 mm airframe gets 1,714.3 m, about 5,600 ft, so 5,500 ft is met within a couple of percent.
0.856 kg liftoff, 22.4:1 thrust-to-weight, rail exit 31.6 m/s, landing 5.2 m/s on a 0.8 m chute, margin 1.59 cal.
Three drafts got here: the 33 mm hull flew to 2,190 m, the H242T in a 44 mm hull reached 1,444 m with a 0.16 cal margin, and the final 41 mm hull reached 1,714 m.
