Two 24.9 mm stages: a C6-5 sustainer 0.30 m long and a 0.22 m booster on a C6 with a 3 s delay (C6-3), not the C6-5 you asked for. The booster separates at burnout and the sustainer lights 0.17 s later. It reaches 647.7 m, about 1.2% above your 2,100 ft.
Both stages land under your 18 ft/s limit: sustainer 3.7 m/s and booster 3.9 m/s, each on a 0.25 m chute. Margin 1.73 cal at rail exit, 1.23 through the boost, rail exit 17.3 m/s.
The 15 g of ballast in the booster is what sets the height, not weight in the sustainer. I did not test heavier builds, and rail exit is only 15% above the gate, so weigh it before flying.
