AeroTech K700W in a 57.5 mm airframe gets 3,661.4 m, so the 3,500 m floor is beaten on the first draft.
3.09 kg liftoff, 22.7:1 thrust-to-weight, rail exit 31.5 m/s, landing 3.4 m/s on a 2.0 m chute, margin 1.58 cal.
The simulator warns that body calculations may not be accurate at supersonic speeds, and the peak is Mach 1.74. The margin over the floor is only 4.6%, so if you need certainty, step up to the 2,437 N*s Cesaroni K in the same diameter (not simulated here).
