A 57.5 mm rocket on AeroTech K550W reaches 3,241.7 m, about 10,600 ft, so 9,000 ft is beaten by about 18%. The simulator warns that body calculations may not be accurate at supersonic speeds (peak Mach 1.56).
2.45 kg liftoff with 0.20 kg of nose ballast, 22.3:1 thrust-to-weight, rail exit 27.1 m/s, landing 3.7 m/s on a 1.7 m chute, margin 1.06 cal.
Since you said you are new: by my recall of the usual certification rules, a K needs Level 2 and a mentor, not a first Level 1 flight. I did not simulate an H or I design for this target, so I cannot say how high those go.
